{"parentUuid":"dc25ef9d-efc3-4084-b83b-c65ed968107c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"7bbfa7a0-a194-4f1f-93d9-ca26bfc18685","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NCcM4JfA1L5oKYN4PJ78d7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Local Offload Orchestrator — the Claude↔Benny contract\n2\t\n3\t> Goal: route the bulk of _execution_ to the local model (Benny) so Claude's\n4\t> tokens/credits are spent on **planning, strategy, and adjudication** — not on\n5\t> typing out boilerplate and reading verbose output back.\n6\t\n7\t## The one insight that shapes everything\n8\t\n9\tOffloading _execution_ to a local model does **not** save tokens on its own. The\n10\texpensive resource is tokens flowing **through the planner's context** — so the\n11\tsavings come from three disciplines, not from \"Benny ran the command\":\n12\t\n13\t1. The planner writes a **compact manifest** instead of doing the work.\n14\t2. An **evaluation gate** absorbs verbose output **locally**.\n15\t3. The planner reads back only a **digest + verdict**, and is pulled in only on\n16\t   failure or ambiguity (**escalation**).\n17\t\n18\tIf the planner reads the full output back, you saved nothing. Digest discipline\n19\tis the product.\n20\t\n21\t## The routing rule\n22\t\n23\t**If you can write crisp, testable acceptance criteria up front, the task is\n24\toffloadable. If defining \"done\" needs judgment, the planner keeps it.**\n25\t\n26\t| Tier      | What                                                               | Handling                                  |\n27\t| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------- |\n28\t| 🟢 green  | scaffolds, codemods, test stubs, doc-gen, formatting, dep bumps    | deterministic gate only, auto-pass        |\n29\t| 🟡 yellow | feature against a spec, bug fix with a repro, multi-file edit      | deterministic gate **+ LLM judge**        |\n30\t| 🔴 red    | architecture, ambiguous reqs, security/signing, deterministic zone | **escalate to planner — never offloaded** |\n31\t\n32\t`router.matrix.json` encodes this and may **upgrade** a declared tier (it never\n33\tsilently downgrades). Touching `L1/ L2/ manifests/` or signing keys forces red.\n34\t\n35\t## The gate (cheapest check first)\n36\t\n37\t1. **Deterministic** (free): `eval_plan.deterministic` commands + every\n38\t   acceptance-criterion `verify`. Every one must exit 0. Most failures stop here.\n39\t2. **LLM judge** (yellow only, only if deterministic passed): scores the result\n40\t   against `acceptance_criteria`, returns `score` + `rationale`.\n41\t3. **Planner adjudication**: only on gate failure (budget exhausted) or\n42\t   low-confidence, per `escalation_policy`.\n43\t\n44\t⚠️ **Anti-collusion:** the judge model SHOULD differ from the executor model.\n45\tSame-model self-judging rubber-stamps. Every judgment is anchored by the\n46\tdeterministic checks regardless — the judge can never _override_ a red gate.\n47\t\n48\t## ADR-001 boundary (why this is safe)\n49\t\n50\tBenny's executor writes only into the workspace **offload scratch** zone\n51\t(`$BENNY_HOME/workspaces/<ws>/offload/`), never the deterministic zone. Promotion\n52\tof a passing result into `manifests/` / L1 / L2 remains a **human-signed** step —\n53\texactly the existing `drafts/ → HITL → sign_manifest()` flow. The gate is the\n54\tmachine pre-filter in front of that human gate, not a replacement for it.\n55\t\n56\t## Files\n57\t\n58\t- `task.manifest.schema.json` — `aamp.offload_task/1` JSON Schema (the contract).\n59\t- `router.matrix.json` — `aamp.offload_router/1` risk matrix + upgrade signals.\n60\t- `examples/green-format-imports.task.json` — true green: `shell` codemod, acts in\n61\t  place, deterministic-only.\n62\t- `examples/yellow-bugfix.task.json` — `generate` task judged against criteria.\n63\t\n64\t### `shell` vs `generate` — which the gate can actually validate\n65\t\n66\tA **`shell`** task acts _in place_, so the deterministic gate validates the real\n67\teffect → it can be true green (deterministic-only). A **`generate`** task produces\n68\tan _unapplied proposal_ in the outbox (ADR-001 — it never touches the live file),\n69\tso deterministic checks run against the _unchanged_ repo and cannot validate it.\n70\tThe router therefore **upgrades every generate task to yellow** and the gate\n71\t**refuses to auto-pass** a generate proposal without a judge — the judge reads the\n72\tartifact text directly and is the only valid evaluator for unapplied output.\n73\t\n74\t## Lanes\n75\t\n76\t- **Sync (MCP):** `offload_exec` tool → `POST /api/offload/submit?wait=1` →\n77\t  returns a compact digest inline. For small bounded tasks the planner needs now.\n78\t- **Async (queue):** drop a manifest in the inbox → `scripts/offload-runner.mjs`\n79\t  drains it → results land in the outbox → planner notified with a digest. The\n80\t  default for bulk work.\n81\t\n82\t## Honesty\n83\t\n84\tPer the memo-ray token-audit lesson: **measure** the savings, don't assert them.\n85\t`scripts/offload-report.mjs` reads the ledger and reports\n86\t_planner-tokens-saved-estimate_, local pass-rate, and escalation rate. Do not\n87\tclaim \"75% offloaded\" until the ledger shows it.\n88\t\n89\tSee `runtime/architecture/ADR-004-local-offload-orchestrator.md` for the full design.\n90\t"}]},"uuid":"7b7724a5-a1d2-49b4-b803-585b26bf3f5c","timestamp":"2026-07-02T08:34:43.856Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\manifests\\offload\\README.md","content":"# Local Offload Orchestrator — the Claude↔Benny contract\n\n> Goal: route the bulk of _execution_ to the local model (Benny) so Claude's\n> tokens/credits are spent on **planning, strategy, and adjudication** — not on\n> typing out boilerplate and reading verbose output back.\n\n## The one insight that shapes everything\n\nOffloading _execution_ to a local model does **not** save tokens on its own. The\nexpensive resource is tokens flowing **through the planner's context** — so the\nsavings come from three disciplines, not from \"Benny ran the command\":\n\n1. The planner writes a **compact manifest** instead of doing the work.\n2. An **evaluation gate** absorbs verbose output **locally**.\n3. The planner reads back only a **digest + verdict**, and is pulled in only on\n   failure or ambiguity (**escalation**).\n\nIf the planner reads the full output back, you saved nothing. Digest discipline\nis the product.\n\n## The routing rule\n\n**If you can write crisp, testable acceptance criteria up front, the task is\noffloadable. If defining \"done\" needs judgment, the planner keeps it.**\n\n| Tier      | What                                                               | Handling                                  |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------- |\n| 🟢 green  | scaffolds, codemods, test stubs, doc-gen, formatting, dep bumps    | deterministic gate only, auto-pass        |\n| 🟡 yellow | feature against a spec, bug fix with a repro, multi-file edit      | deterministic gate **+ LLM judge**        |\n| 🔴 red    | architecture, ambiguous reqs, security/signing, deterministic zone | **escalate to planner — never offloaded** |\n\n`router.matrix.json` encodes this and may **upgrade** a declared tier (it never\nsilently downgrades). Touching `L1/ L2/ manifests/` or signing keys forces red.\n\n## The gate (cheapest check first)\n\n1. **Deterministic** (free): `eval_plan.deterministic` commands + every\n   acceptance-criterion `verify`. Every one must exit 0. Most failures stop here.\n2. **LLM judge** (yellow only, only if deterministic passed): scores the result\n   against `acceptance_criteria`, returns `score` + `rationale`.\n3. **Planner adjudication**: only on gate failure (budget exhausted) or\n   low-confidence, per `escalation_policy`.\n\n⚠️ **Anti-collusion:** the judge model SHOULD differ from the executor model.\nSame-model self-judging rubber-stamps. Every judgment is anchored by the\ndeterministic checks regardless — the judge can never _override_ a red gate.\n\n## ADR-001 boundary (why this is safe)\n\nBenny's executor writes only into the workspace **offload scratch** zone\n(`$BENNY_HOME/workspaces/<ws>/offload/`), never the deterministic zone. Promotion\nof a passing result into `manifests/` / L1 / L2 remains a **human-signed** step —\nexactly the existing `drafts/ → HITL → sign_manifest()` flow. The gate is the\nmachine pre-filter in front of that human gate, not a replacement for it.\n\n## Files\n\n- `task.manifest.schema.json` — `aamp.offload_task/1` JSON Schema (the contract).\n- `router.matrix.json` — `aamp.offload_router/1` risk matrix + upgrade signals.\n- `examples/green-format-imports.task.json` — true green: `shell` codemod, acts in\n  place, deterministic-only.\n- `examples/yellow-bugfix.task.json` — `generate` task judged against criteria.\n\n### `shell` vs `generate` — which the gate can actually validate\n\nA **`shell`** task acts _in place_, so the deterministic gate validates the real\neffect → it can be true green (deterministic-only). A **`generate`** task produces\nan _unapplied proposal_ in the outbox (ADR-001 — it never touches the live file),\nso deterministic checks run against the _unchanged_ repo and cannot validate it.\nThe router therefore **upgrades every generate task to yellow** and the gate\n**refuses to auto-pass** a generate proposal without a judge — the judge reads the\nartifact text directly and is the only valid evaluator for unapplied output.\n\n## Lanes\n\n- **Sync (MCP):** `offload_exec` tool → `POST /api/offload/submit?wait=1` →\n  returns a compact digest inline. For small bounded tasks the planner needs now.\n- **Async (queue):** drop a manifest in the inbox → `scripts/offload-runner.mjs`\n  drains it → results land in the outbox → planner notified with a