n step. The TOGAF swarm manifest is executed\nby the operator (`benny run`), not by an agent.\n\n## 10. Status / verification\n\n- Pilot (5 sessions, mixed agents) through live Lemonade `qwen3.5-9b-FLM`:\n  see §Pilot results appended after the run — throughput figures there are the\n  extrapolation basis for the full backlog; nothing is claimed beyond them.\n- Full-backlog rate, judge-free quality rate at volume, and delta-mode cadence\n  are **unverified until the ledger shows them**.\n\n## 11. Consequences\n\n- 9 months of history becomes a queryable graph + cited deliverables, produced\n  for electricity, refreshed incrementally.\n- New surface: `scripts/longview/` runner + prompts (small, no new deps) and a\n  session-card schema to maintain.\n- Risks: 9B synthesis quality ceiling (mitigated: citations make weak cards\n  visible and re-runnable per-session); OneDrive sync churn on the workspace\n  (mitigated: ledger appends, not rewrites); protobuf conversations remain\n  unread (accepted: artifacts + transcripts carry the signal; a .pb decoder is\n  future work).\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e62b5a55-3f94-40c8-b195-a1e38de31213","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"79f3f47a-9f9d-4a1f-b922-ef7b2aa390a9","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
