{"parentUuid":"d697414e-ec2b-4661-8433-ac2e9c135665","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_01BMQy68ECENX51KyheVT83P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RxF7uCrGk9TqqQxFWKyN9z","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\scripts\\longview\\README.md","content":"# LONGVIEW — long-horizon session synthesis (ADR-005)\n\nTurns 9 months of local agent sessions (Antigravity brain + Claude Code, via the\nmemo-ray entity store) into a queryable knowledge graph and cited deliverables —\na portfolio report, a PRD for what comes next, an operator skill, a book, and a\nTOGAF SAD — all generated by the local model (Lemonade `qwen3.5-9b-FLM`), for\nelectricity instead of tokens.\n\nDesign: `runtime/architecture/ADR-005-longview-session-synthesis.md`.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- Lemonade serving on `:13305` with `qwen3.5-9b-FLM` (or set `LONGVIEW_MODEL`).\n- Benny runtime on `:8005` (only needed for Phase D graph ingestion + TOGAF run).\n- memo-ray checkout as a sibling of prime-silo (or set `MEMORAY_DATA_DIR`);\n  its server running is optional — sync falls back to invoking the parsers.\n\n## The backlog run (leave it overnight)\n\n```powershell\ncd prime-silo\nnode scripts/longview/longview.mjs all\n```\n\nResume-safe at card granularity: Ctrl+C anytime, rerun the same command, it\ncontinues where the ledger says it stopped. Progress:\n\n```powershell\nnode scripts/longview/longview.mjs status   # live heartbeat (phase, ETA, rates)\nnode scripts/longview/longview.mjs report   # honest ledger report\n```\n\n## The delta run (keeping it current)\n\n```powershell\nnode scripts/longview/longview.mjs delta            # only new/changed sessions\nnode scripts/longview/longview.mjs delta --refresh  # force deliverable re-synthesis\n```\n\nReduce re-runs automatically once ≥5 new cards accumulate (`LONGVIEW_DELTA_THRESHOLD`).\n\n## Phases (runnable individually)\n\n| Phase     | Command       | What                                                        | LLM? |\n| --------- | ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- | ---- |\n| inventory | `inventory`   | memo-ray sync + session census                              | no   |\n| extract   | `extract`     | deterministic evidence packs (≤9 KB each)                   | no   |\n| map       | `map`         | evidence → session cards, gated + ledgered (the long part)  | yes  |\n| model     | `model`       | rollups + cards into the workspace knowledge graph          | no*  |\n| reduce    | `reduce`      | dossiers → themes → report/PRD/skill/book (+ TOGAF prep)    | yes  |\n\n\\* `model` calls Benny `/rag/ingest`, which embeds locally. Skip with `--no-graph`.\n\n## Where things land\n\n```\n$BENNY_HOME/workspaces/longview/\n├── longview/            state: inventory, evidence/, cards/, rollups/,\n│                        ledger.jsonl (honesty), status.json (heartbeat)\n├── data_in/             session-card markdown (graph corpus)\n└── data_out/            deliverables:\n    ├── PORTFOLIO-REPORT.md, THEMES.md, PRD-WHAT-COMES-NEXT.md\n    ├── dossiers/<project>.md, skills/working-with-this-operator.SKILL.md\n    ├── book/BOOK.md (+ outline.json, chapter-NN.md)\n    └── TOGAF-RUN.md     the human-launched SAD swarm command (ADR-001)\n```\n\nDeliverables are proposals in `data_out/` — promoting a skill into\n`~/.claude/skills`, or the PRD into the roadmap, stays a human step.\n\n## Observability\n\n- `status.json` — updated after every card; Bridge's file browser can watch it.\n- `ledger.jsonl` — append-only; `report` reads only this. Numbers not in the\n  ledger don't get claimed (memo-ray token-audit lesson).\n- Phase D ingestion and the TOGAF swarm run in the Benny runtime ⇒ visible in\n  Mission Control / the activity feed like any other run.\n- Lemonade's own console shows live generation.\n\n## Honest limitations (v1)\n\n- 63 of 130 indexed sessions are \"thin\" (empty brain dirs; conversations exist\n  only as unparsed protobuf). They are ledgered `skipped_thin`, not guessed at.\n  A `.pb` decoder or the `antigravity-backup/` dirs would raise coverage.\n- Claude coverage in the memo-ray store is 7 sessions vs 36 transcript files on\n  disk — worth a look at `claudeParser` thresholds.\n- Card quality has a 9B ceiling; every claim carries session-id citations so\n  weak cards are visible and re-runnable (`map --force` after deleting a card).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":342,"cache_read_input_tokens":169304,"output_tokens":1901,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":342,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1901,"cache_read_input_tokens":169304,"cache_creation_input_tokens":342,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":342},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CccwzJo3KzFjKYKbyVAjt","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_session","attributionMcpTool":"mark_chapter","type":"assistant","uuid":"4cf99cf9-270c-4eba-a7b4-37cc8e4cb6f3","timestamp":"2026-07-02T08:54:23.548Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo","sessionId":"79f3f47a-9f9d-4a1f-b922-ef7b2aa390a9","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
