{"parentUuid":"57778b4d-5f2c-4740-b395-be658fab1c9d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_017QeUr5QZsmEPAt9Ru8XEfK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The workflow is designed, built, and proven live end to end. Here's the full picture.\n\n## What got built\n\n**LONGVIEW** (ADR: [ADR-005-longview-session-synthesis.md](prime-silo/runtime/architecture/ADR-005-longview-session-synthesis.md), code: [scripts/longview/](prime-silo/scripts/longview/README.md)) — a map-reduce pipeline that turns your session history into a queryable graph plus cited deliverables, run entirely on `qwen3.5-9b-FLM` through Lemonade. You were right about memo-ray: its entity store already normalizes all four agents with per-agent sync watermarks, so LONGVIEW does zero session parsing of its own — memo-ray is the ingestion seam, and adding an agent later is a memo-ray parser, not a pipeline change.\n\n**Greater than the sum works through three deliberate mechanisms.** Vertical: the ladder (evidence → card → dossier → theme → deliverable) means the 9B model never sees more than one bounded context, yet the top rung is transitively conditioned on everything, with session-id citations at every rung so any claim traces back to a real session. Horizontal: cards ingest into the workspace knowledge graph, where concepts recurring across projects surface themes no single session contains — and the TOGAF swarm's baseline step queries that graph, so the SAD describes the estate, not one repo. Temporal: cards carry periods, so the book and PRD read the nine-month arc, not snapshots.\n\n## Pilot results (all ledger-sourced)\n\n- 8 sessions processed: **4 cards ok, 0 gate failures, 4 thin-skipped** (empty brain dirs, honestly recorded rather than hallucinated)\n- 54–116s per card warm ≈ **44 cards/hour → ~2.8 hours for the remaining 122-session backlog** — much better than feared\n- Kill/resume verified; graph ingestion landed 40 chunks (runtime run visible in Mission Control); semantic query returns cited chunks\n- Real deliverables generated: two project dossiers, THEMES.md, and `working-with-this-operator.SKILL.md` — the skill correctly distilled things like \"validate with metrics, not qualitative claims\" from just 4 cards\n\n## To leave running\n\n```powershell\ncd C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\nnode scripts/longview/longview.mjs all        # full backlog, ~3-4h, Ctrl+C safe\nnode scripts/longview/longview.mjs status     # heartbeat: phase, ETA, rates\nnode scripts/longview/longview.mjs report     # honest ledger report\nnode scripts/longview/longview.mjs delta      # afterwards: keep it current\n```\n\nDeliverables land in the runtime's `workspaces/longview/data_out/`, including `TOGAF-RUN.md` with the exact human-launched swarm command.\n\n## Honest caveats\n\nLemonade serves qwen3.5 at **ctx 4096** — raising it to 16k+ (then bumping `LONGVIEW_EVIDENCE_BUDGET`/`LONGVIEW_REDUCE_INPUT`) is the single biggest quality lever for the full run. The runtime's home resolves to `%APPDATA%\\space-agent\\benny-home\\benny`, not the repo `.benny_home` — found and fixed during the pilot. Claude is undercounted in the store (7 of 36 transcripts) — I've flagged a chip to fix `claudeParser`; run `delta` after and the recovered sessions flow through automatically. The 104 `antigravity-backup` brain dirs are one config line away from inclusion. Report/PRD/book quality at full corpus size is unverified until the ledger shows it."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":88,"cache_read_input_tokens":242521,"output_tokens":1266,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":88,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1266,"cache_read_input_tokens":242521,"cache