               # honest ledger report\n```\n\n(Equivalent direct form: `node scripts/longview/longview.mjs run [manifest] [--phase X] [--delta]`.)\nPer ADR-005 §4 the manifest's tasks are the five *phases* — the per-session\nfan-out stays inside the map phase's checkpointed loop, never as swarm tasks.\nEdit the manifest to change model, budgets, batch sizes, or to disable phases.\n\nResume-safe at card granularity: Ctrl+C anytime, rerun the same command, it\ncontinues where the ledger says it stopped. Delta reduce re-runs automatically\nonce ≥5 new cards accumulate (`delta_reduce_threshold`).\n\n## Graph ingestion (deep synthesis)\n\n`deep_synthesis: true` in the manifest is what turns card docs into\nDocument/Concept nodes in Neo4j — without it `/rag/ingest` writes **vectors\nonly** and the knowledge-graph views stay empty (found live: 55 cards in\nChroma, zero graph nodes). Synthesis is LLM-per-document, so ingest batches\nare small (`ingest_batch_size: 5`) and slow; the phase is idempotent (old\nvectors per source are deleted before re-add), so re-running `--phase model`\nafter clearing `longview/rollups/ingested.json` back-fills the graph.","originalFile":"# LONGVIEW — long-horizon session synthesis (ADR-005)\n\nTurns 9 months of local agent sessions (Antigravity brain + Claude Code, via the\nmemo-ray entity store) into a queryable knowledge graph and cited deliverables —\na portfolio report, a PRD for what comes next, an operator skill, a book, and a\nTOGAF SAD — all generated by the local model (Lemonade `qwen3.5-9b-FLM`), for\nelectricity instead of tokens.\n\nDesign: `runtime/architecture/ADR-005-longview-session-synthesis.md`.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- Lemonade serving on `:13305` with `qwen3.5-9b-FLM` (or set `LONGVIEW_MODEL`).\n  The FLM recipe currently loads with `ctx_size 4096`, which caps evidence packs\n  at 7500 chars and reduce inputs at 8500 chars (both enforced). **Raising the\n  FLM ctx_size to 16384+** and setting `LONGVIEW_EVIDENCE_BUDGET=12000` /\n  `LONGVIEW_REDUCE_INPUT=30000` buys noticeably higher-fidelity synthesis.\n- Benny runtime on `:8005` (only needed for Phase D graph ingestion + TOGAF run).\n  The workspace lives under the **runtime's resolved home** (desktop config →\n  `%APPDATA%\\space-agent\\benny-home\\benny` on this box) — `lib/config.mjs`\n  resolves it with `packaging/desktop/home_resolver.js`, same as the runtime.\n- memo-ray checkout as a sibling of prime-silo (or set `MEMORAY_DATA_DIR`);\n  its server running is optional — sync falls back to invoking the parsers.\n\n## The backlog run (leave it overnight)\n\n```powershell\ncd prime-silo\nnode scripts/longview/longview.mjs all\n```\n\nResume-safe at card granularity: Ctrl+C anytime, rerun the same command, it\ncontinues where the ledger says it stopped. Progress:\n\n```powershell\nnode scripts/longview/longview.mjs status   # live heartbeat (phase, ETA, rates)\nnode scripts/longview/longview.mjs report   # honest ledger report\n```\n\n## The delta run (keeping it current)\n\n```powershell\nnode scripts/longview/longview.mjs delta            # only new/changed sessions\nnode scripts/longview/longview.mjs delta --refresh  # force deliverable re-synthesis\n```\n\nReduce re-runs automatically once ≥5 new cards accumulate (`LONGVIEW_DELTA_THRESHOLD`).\n\n## Phases (runnable individually)\n\n| Phase     | Command       | What                                                        | LLM? |\n| --------- | ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- | ---- |\n| inventory | `inventory`   | memo-ray sync + session census                              | no   |\n| extract   | `extract`     | deterministic evidence packs (≤9 KB each)                   | no   |\n| map       | `map`         | evidence → session cards, gated + ledgered (the long part)  | yes  |\n| model     | `model`       | rollups + cards into the workspace knowledge graph          | no*  |\n| reduce    | `reduce`      | dossiers → themes → report/PRD/skill/book (+ TOGAF prep)    | yes  |\n\n\\* `model` calls Benny `/rag/ingest`, which embeds locally. Skip with `--no-graph`.\n\n## Where things land\n\n```\n$BENNY_HOME/workspaces/longview/\n├── longview/            state: inventory, evidence/, cards/, rollups/,\n│                        ledger.jsonl (honesty), status.json (heartbeat)\n├── data_in/             session-card markdown (graph corpus)\n└── data_out/            deliverables:\n    ├── PORTFOLIO-REPORT.md, THEMES.md, PRD-WHAT-COMES-NEXT.md\n    ├── dossiers/<project>.md, skills/working-with-this-operator.SKILL.md\n    ├── book/BOOK.md (+ outline.json, chapter-NN.md)\n    └── TOGAF-RUN.md     the human-launched SAD swarm command (ADR-001)\n```\n\nDeliverables are proposals in `data_out/` — promoting a skill into\n`~/.claude/skills`, or the PRD into the roadmap, stays a human step.\n\n## Observability\n\n- `status.json` — updated after every card; Bridge's file browser can watch it.\n- `ledger.jsonl` — append-only; `report` reads only this. Numbers not in the\n  ledger don't get claimed (memo-ray token-audit lesson).\n- Phase D ingestion and the TOGAF swarm run in the Benny runtime ⇒ visible in\n  Mission Control / the activity feed like any other run.\n- Lemonade's own console shows live generation.\n\n## Honest limitations (v1)\n\n- 63 of 130 indexed sessions are \"thin\" (empty brain dirs; conversations exist\n  only as unparsed protobuf). They are ledgered `skipped_thin`, not guessed at.\n  A `.pb` decoder or the `antigravity-backup/` dirs would raise coverage.\n- Claude coverage in the memo-ray store is 7 sessions vs 36 transcript files on\n  disk — worth a look at `claudeParser` thresholds.\n- Card quality has a 9B ceiling; every claim carries session-id citations so\n  weak cards are visible and re-runnable (`map --force` after deleting a card).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":22,"oldLines":30,"newStart":22,"newLines":40,"lines":[" - memo-ray checkout as a sibling of prime-silo (or set `MEMORAY_DATA_DIR`);","   its server running is optional — sync falls back to invoking the parsers."," ","-## The backlog run (leave it overnight)","+## Manifest mode (the managed way — use this)"," ","-```powershell","-cd prime-silo","-node scripts/longview/longview.mjs all","-```","+The pipeline definition of record is","+`runtime/manifests/templates/longview_synthesis.json` (variables + phases).","+Run and manage it from the Benny CLI:"," ","-Resume-safe at card granularity: Ctrl+C anytime, rerun the same command, it","-continues where the ledger says it stopped. Progress:","-"," ```powershell","-node scripts/longview/longview.mjs status   # live heartbeat (phase, ETA, rates)","-node scripts/longview/longview.mjs report   # honest ledger report","+cd prime-silo/runtime","+python benny_cli.py longview run                  # all enabled phases, resume-safe","+python benny_cli.py longview run --phase model    # one phase","+python benny_cli.py longview run --delta          # only new/changed sessions","+python benny_cli.py longview status               # live heartbeat (phase, ETA, rates)","+python benny_cli.py longview report               # honest ledger report"," ```"," ","-## The delta run (keeping it current)","+(Equivalent direct form: `node scripts/longview/longview.mjs run [manifest] [--phase X] [--delta]`.)","+Per ADR-005 §4 the manifest's tasks are the five *phases* — the per-session","+fan-out stays inside the map phase's checkpointed loop, never as swarm tasks.","+Edit the manifest to change model, budgets, batch sizes, or to disable phases."," ","-```powershell","-node scripts/longview/longview.mjs delta            # only new/changed sessions","-node scripts/longview/longview.mjs delta --refresh  # force deliverable re-synthesis","-```","+Resume-safe at card granularity: Ctrl+C anytime, rerun the same command, it","+continues where the ledger says it stopped. Delta reduce re-runs automatically","+once ≥5 new cards accumulate (`delta_reduce_threshold`)."," ","-Reduce re-runs automatically once ≥5 new cards accumulate (`LONGVIEW_DELTA_THRESHOLD`).","+## Graph ingestion (deep synthesis)"," ","+`deep_synthesis: true` in the manifest is what turns card docs into","+Document/Concept nodes in Neo4j — without it `/rag/ingest` writes **vectors","+only** and the knowledge-graph views stay empty (found live: 55 cards in","+Chroma, zero graph nodes). Synthesis is LLM-per-document, so ingest batches","+are small (`ingest_batch_size: 5`) and slow; the phase is idempotent (old","+vectors per source are deleted before re-add), so re-running `--phase model`","+after clearing `longview/rollups/ingested.json` back-fills the graph.","+"," ## Phases (runnable individually)"," "," | Phase     | Command       | What                                                        | LLM? |"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"95f039ab-4348-436b-b6d8-d6903d540258","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\runtime","sessionId":"79f3f47a-9f9d-4a1f-b922-ef7b2aa390a9","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
