s.json)** — the definition of record: variables (model, budgets, `deep_synthesis`, batch sizes) + the five phases as plan tasks. Edit it to reconfigure; no code changes needed.\n- **`benny longview run [--phase X] [--delta] | status | report`** — new CLI subcommand in `benny_cli.py`, tested working. `--phase map` will also retry the 12 failed cards.\n- One deliberate boundary, documented in ADR-005: the manifest's tasks are the *phases*, never the 300 sessions — the swarm executor has no shell step and the 45-task TOGAF blowup showed why fan-out inside a manifest fails. Runtime-executed steps (ingestion, the TOGAF swarm) appear in `benny runs ls` as real runs; the map loop keeps its own ledger. If you want the whole manifest run in run history, the identified follow-up is a small `/api/longview` route that registers into `run_store`.\n\n## From the earlier \"continue\" — EXE visibility fixed in the repo\n\nThree layers hid your outputs: the files API silently skipped directories (now recursive for `data_out` — `skills\\working-with-this-operator.SKILL.md` lists correctly, verified against your real workspace), Bridge had no outputs view at all (new read-only **Outputs** section in Documents, verified end-to-end on the dev shell at `http://127.0.0.1:3100` — file list → click → 200), and the tray now has one **Home** submenu with **Open workspaces (runs & outputs)** as the first entry. These reach the installed EXE with the next release build; until then the dev shell shows them."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1150,"cache_read_input_tokens":382716,"output_tokens":1217,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1150,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1217,"cache_read_input_tokens":382716,"cache_creation_inpu