raph + report/PRD/skill/book/TOGAF SAD; backlog + delta modes\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 79f3f47a-9f9d-4a1f-b922-ef7b2aa390a9\n---\n\nLONGVIEW workflow (designed + piloted 2026-07-02), ADR at prime-silo/runtime/architecture/ADR-005-longview-session-synthesis.md, code at prime-silo/scripts/longview/ (Node, no new deps), workspace `.benny_home/workspaces/longview/`.\n\n**Shape**: map-reduce over the memo-ray entity store (the seam — its 4 parsers + per-agent sync watermarks do all session parsing; LONGVIEW parses nothing). Phases: inventory (memo-ray sync) → extract (deterministic ≤9KB evidence packs) → map (qwen3.5-9b-FLM via lemonade:13305 → gated session cards, resume-safe ledger) → model (rollups + /rag/ingest into workspace graph) → reduce (dossiers → themes → PORTFOLIO-REPORT, PRD, operator SKILL.md, book, TOGAF-RUN.md prep reusing togaf_sad_report_swarm.json). `delta` command re-maps only new/changed sessions; reduce auto-reruns at ≥5 new cards.\n\n**Key decisions**: MAP is a purpose-built loop, NOT ADR-004 offload tasks (prose judge false-escalates; card acceptance is deterministically checkable = green-tier; 45-task fan-out lesson). REDUCE reuses bounded swarm manifests where possible (observability via EventBus). Grounding chain: deliverable→dossier→card→evidence→session, session-id citations enforced by prompts + gate.\n\n**Data reality (2026-07-02)**: Antigravity brain at ~/.gemini/antigravity/brain (111 dirs, 852MB; +104 in antigravity-backup NOT in memo-ray config); conversations are protobuf (unparsed, 305MB); only 6 have transcript.jsonl; 115 md artifacts. memo-ray store: 130 sessions (123 AG + 7 Claude — Claude undercounts vs 36 jsonl on disk, parser needs a look). 63/130 sessions thin (<200 chars extractable) → ledgered skipped_thin, not guessed.\n\n**Observability**: workspace longview/status.json heartbeat + ledger.jsonl (only source of reported numbers) + `longview.mjs report`. EventBus has NO external publish surface — MAP loop can't feed the activity chip in v1. Phase D /rag/ingest + TOGAF swarm DO run in the runtime → visible in Mission Control.\n\n**Pilot verified (2026-07-02)**: 4 cards ok / 0 failed / 4 thin-skipped through live qwen3.5-9b-FLM (NPU): 144s cold, 54-77s warm ≈ 39 cards/hour → full 130-session backlog ≈ 3.2h. Resume (ledger skip) verified. /rag/ingest landed 40 chunks/4 docs in longview collection (run 16fe485c).\n\n**Gotchas learned**: (1) the RUNNING runtime's home ≠ repo .benny_home — it resolves via desktop config to `%APPDATA%\\space-agent\\benny-home\\benny`; any script hitting runtime APIs must resolve via packaging/desktop/home_resolver.js (LONGVIEW config.mjs does). (2) lemonade serves qwen3.5-9b-FLM with ctx_size 4096 → evidence budget capped at 7500 chars; raise FLM ctx to raise budget. (3) render≠ingest — track ingested files explicitly (rollups/ingested.json). (4) memo-ray store undercounts Claude (7 of 36 jsonl) — spawned fix task. (5) **`/rag/ingest` defaults `deep_synthesis: false`** → vectors land in Chroma but Neo4j graph stays EMPTY; a 6-second multi-file \"ingest ok\" is the tell. Always pass deep_synthesis+model; small batches (5) + 30-min timeout.\n\n**RELEASED as v1.9.0 (2026-07-02)**: commit 80467ea + tag v1.9.0 pushed, Release Desktop CI building. Operator guides added: runtime/docs/operations/{LONGVIEW_GUIDE,TOGAF_SAD_SWARM_GUIDE,VISION_INGESTION_GUIDE}.md + INDEX/CLI/CLAUDE wiring. Ingest client is fire-and-poll (undici kills held connections ~5min; poll /api/tasks for run_id until completed/failed/completed_with_errors). Graph re-ingest of all 55 cards left running unattended post-release.\n\n**Full backlog run (2026-07-02)**: 130 sessions → 55 cards / 12 failed / 63 thin, 51.9 cards/h, 17 projects, 34 reduce artifacts. **Manifest mode added** (user wants CLI-managed): `runtime/manifests/templates/longview_synthesis.json` (phases as tasks, variables incl. deep_synthesis) + `longview.mjs run [--phase|--delta]` + `benny longview run|status|report` CLI subcommand. Swarm executor has no shell step kind + tasks API is read-only → map loop can't register RunRecords; follow-up idea: /api/longview route into run_store. Also fixed EXE visibility: get_workspace_files recursive for data_out, Bridge \"Outputs\" section, tray Home submenu with \"Open workspaces\" (all need next release to reach the EXE).\n\nRelated: [[project-prime-silo-offload-orchestrator]], [[prime-silo-togaf-report-manifest-fixes]], [[memo-ray-token-audit-validation]]\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":21,"oldLines":6,"newStart":21,"newLines":8,"lines":[" "," **Gotchas learned**: (1) the RUNNING runtime's home ≠ repo .benny_home — it resolves via desktop config to `%APPDATA%\\space-agent\\benny-home\\benny`; any script hitting runtime APIs must resolve via packaging/desktop/home_resolver.js (LONGVIEW config.mjs does). (2) lemonade serves qwen3.5-9b-FLM with ctx_size 4096 → evidence budget capped at 7500 chars; raise FLM ctx to raise budget. (3) render≠ingest — track ingested files explicitly (rollups/ingested.json). (4) memo-ray store undercounts Claude (7 of 36 jsonl) — spawned fix task. (5) **`/rag/ingest` defaults `deep_synthesis: false`** → vectors land in Chroma but Neo4j graph stays EMPTY; a 6-second multi-file \"ingest ok\" is the tell. Always pass deep_synthesis+model; small batches (5) + 30-min timeout."," ","+**v1.9.1 (2026-07-02)**: one-click LONGVIEW from the EXE — packaging/desktop/longview_service.js (single spawn path, ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE so no system Node needed; logs to <ws>/longview/runner.log), server API longview_run/status/stop, Bridge \"LONGVIEW pipeline\" panel (Documents, longview ws: run delta/full/stop + live heartbeat), tray status+run/stop/open-outputs. Runner gained per-workspace lock (stale-pid reclaim) + manifest/memoray-store fallbacks for packaged installs. Verified: spawn e2e (inventory), HTTP status 200, served markup. ALSO: v1.9.0 Lint&Test failed on a PRE-EXISTING parse error — 1.8.2 s