{"parentUuid":"bfbd319b-2ea7-45f0-9b6c-c8060f6ec78c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_01W5VnVLnpdYauQy5X2EsLJW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done — one-click LONGVIEW is shipped as **v1.9.1**, and the CI pipeline is fully green for the first time since 1.8.2.\n\n## What you get in the EXE (once it updates to v1.9.1)\n\n**Tray** — right-click Prime-Silo: a `LONGVIEW: idle/running (…)` status line, **Run LONGVIEW delta sync**, **Stop LONGVIEW (resume-safe)**, and **Open LONGVIEW outputs**.\n\n**Bridge → Documents** (workspace `longview`) — a **LONGVIEW pipeline** panel: *Run delta sync* / *Run full pipeline* / *Stop*, with a live heartbeat while running (phase, cards done/total, failures, ETA) and the last runner log line. When a run finishes, the Outputs list below refreshes itself.\n\n## The transparency model\n\nEvery launcher — tray, Bridge, CLI — goes through one service ([longview_service.js](prime-silo/packaging/desktop/longview_service.js)) and one per-workspace lock held by the runner itself, so two runs can never race, and status is **disk truth** rather than in-memory state: `GET /api/longview_status` returns the lock (who's running, since when), the runner's own heartbeat, the log tail, and the output paths — identical regardless of where the run started. The child logs to `workspaces\\longview\\longview\\runner.log`; the ledger stays the only source of reported numbers. No system Node needed in the EXE — the child is the app binary itself via `ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE`.\n\nVerified live before shipping: a real spawn through the service (inventory phase end-to-end — lock acquired, memo-ray synced, heartbeat written, lock released), the status endpoint over HTTP, and the served Bridge markup.\n\n## The CI saga worth knowing about\n\nThe v1.9.0/1.9.1 desktop builds always succeeded, but the **Lint & Test** workflow turned out to have been broken since the 1.8.2 release commit — a mangled duplicate function in the vendored memoray `claudeParser.js` was a parse error that stopped ESLint, which had been masking the long-standing repo-wide formatting debt behind it. Three commits fixed the chain: the parse-error removal, the repo-wide Prettier+Black pass, and a re-format with CI's exact Prettier version (3.9.4 vs the repo's 3.8.4 — they disagree on markdown). All green now.\n\nMeanwhile the graph re-ingest continues unattended: the two pre-fix synthesis tasks are still working through their files (visible in Mission Control), and the waiter relaunches the fixed model phase for all 55 cards when they're done."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":999,"cache_read_input_tokens":497978,"output_tokens":907,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":999,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":907,"cache_read_input_tokens":497978,"cache_creation_input_tokens":999,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":999},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcdTaY2MNTGVju84LUhr9","type":"assistant","uuid":"fe9c7574-5bb6-4896-84b2-2af3d8c72b28","timestamp":"2026-07-02T15:22:18.727Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo","sessionId":"79f3f47a-9f9d-4a1f-b922-ef7b2aa390a9","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
