{"parentUuid":"363c2711-812a-4769-93e7-842a9ae9a612","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\scripts\\longview\\prompts\\prd.md","snippet":"1\tYou are a product manager writing a PRD for WHAT SHOULD COME NEXT, grounded in months of session evidence (themes + dossier summaries + open threads rollup provided below).\n2\t\n3\tWrite markdown:\n4\t\n5\t# PRD: <a name you choose for the next phase>\n6\t\n7\t## Problem statement\n8\t\n9\tWhat the portfolio evidence says is the real unmet need.\n10\t\n11\t## Goals / Non-goals\n12\t\n13\t## Proposed work\n14\t\n15\t3-6 concrete initiatives. For each: what, why now (cite session ids / open threads), acceptance criteria that are testable, and which existing application it lands in.\n16\t\n17\t## Sequencing and dependencies\n18\t\n19\t## Success metrics\n20\t\n21\tMeasurable, honest — no vanity metrics.\n22\t\n23\t## Risks\n24\t\n25\tRules: every initiative must trace to cited open threads or themes; acceptance criteria must be crisp enough that a local-model executor could be gated on them (ADR-004 routing rule); under 1200 words."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4aac68d4-ec21-4f8b-9741-91864e5ef115","timestamp":"2026-07-02T19:55:29.512Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"79f3f47a-9f9d-4a1f-b922-ef7b2aa390a9","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"4aac68d4-ec21-4f8b-9741-91864e5ef115","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\scripts\\longview\\prompts\\report.md","snippet":"1\tYou are writing the LONGVIEW portfolio report: a detailed, honest account of an operator's estate of applications built with AI coding agents. Inputs: cross-project themes, project dossier summaries, and rollup statistics.\n2\t\n3\tWrite markdown with these sections:\n4\t\n5\t# LONGVIEW Portfolio Report\n6\t\n7\t## Executive summary\n8\t\n9\tWhat exists, what it's for, where it's heading. One page equivalent.\n10\t\n11\t## Applications\n12\t\n13\tOne subsection per application: what it is, maturity, key capabilities. Cite session ids.\n14\t\n15\t## Capability inventory\n16\t\n17\tThe reusable technical capabilities across the estate, grouped (e.g. graph/RAG, release engineering, local-model orchestration). Cite where each was demonstrated.\n18\t\n19\t## What the operator is trying to achieve\n20\t\n21\tSynthesis from the themes input.\n22\t\n23\t## State of play\n24\t\n25\tVerified vs unverified, shipped vs stalled, and the honest gaps.\n26\t\n27\tRules: cite session ids and project names throughout; report only what the inputs support; under 1500 words."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"455bf2fa-78ff-48c9-b474-3ad63db3b159","timestamp":"2026-07-02T19:55:29.512Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"79f3f47a-9f9d-4a1f-b922-ef7b2aa390a9","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
