{"parentUuid":"09baf22f-6caf-4e2d-959b-5d212799db8b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\scripts\\longview\\prompts\\discovery_note.md","snippet":"1\tYou are a research analyst answering one discovery question using retrieved evidence from a knowledge corpus (session cards, project dossiers, prior notes) and graph context. Write a DISCOVERY NOTE in markdown:\n2\t\n3\t# <restate the question as a title>\n4\t\n5\t## Finding\n6\t\n7\tThe answer, argued from the evidence. 2-4 paragraphs. Concrete, specific, honest about uncertainty.\n8\t\n9\t## Evidence\n10\t\n11\tBulleted: each bullet cites its source — session ids like (sid: abc123), document names, or concept names from the graph context.\n12\t\n13\t## Connections\n14\t\n15\tWhat this links to across projects/concepts that wasn't obvious before — the cross-reference value of this note.\n16\t\n17\t## Follow-up\n18\t\n19\t0-2 sharper questions this raises.\n20\t\n21\tRules: only claim what the retrieved evidence supports; never invent sessions or files; keep under 600 words; cite in-line throughout."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"205d20af-2f03-4aac-a01f-4843dc09e6b2","timestamp":"2026-07-02T20:18:20.722Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo","sessionId":"79f3f47a-9f9d-4a1f-b922-ef7b2aa390a9","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"205d20af-2f03-4aac-a01f-4843dc09e6b2","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\scripts\\longview\\prompts\\discovery_questions.md","snippet":"1\tYou are a research director running a discovery loop over a knowledge graph built from months of software-engineering sessions. Below: current themes, capability rollup, and the titles of discovery notes already written. Your job: find what is UNDER-EXPLORED — cross-project connections, contradictions, evolution patterns, or architecture questions the current documents do not answer.\n2\t\n3\tReturn ONLY a JSON object:\n4\t\n5\t{\n6\t\"questions\": [\n7\t{ \"id\": \"q1\", \"question\": \"a sharp, specific question answerable from the corpus\", \"why\": \"what new understanding this unlocks\" }\n8\t]\n9\t}\n10\t\n11\tRules: exactly the requested number of questions; each must be answerable from session evidence (not speculation about the future); avoid questions already covered by existing notes; prefer questions that CONNECT multiple projects or connect code structure to decisions. JSON only."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9d30515b-f167-419c-a304-a9e5b3805d09","timestamp":"2026-07-02T20:18:20.723Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo","sessionId":"79f3f47a-9f9d-4a1f-b922-ef7b2aa390a9","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"9d30515b-f167-419c-a304-a9e5b3805d09","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\scripts\\longview\\prompts\\vampire_chapter_sections.md","snippet":"1\tYou are the structural editor of \"The AI Vampire\" (narrative nonfiction, senior software engineer × multi-agent coordination). Given the book outline, ONE chapter's spec, and the evidence available, break this chapter into sections.\n2\t\n3\tReturn ONLY a JSON object:\n4\t\n5\t{\n6\t\"sections\": [\n7\t{\n8\t\"id\": \"p1c2s3\",\n9\t\"title\": \"...\",\n10\t\"brief\": \"2-3 sentences: what this section narrates/argues and how it advances the chapter\",\n11\t\"query\": \"a retrieval query (plain text) that will fetch the best supporting evidence from the corpus for this section\"\n12\t}\n13\t]\n14\t}\n15\t\n16\tRules: 5-7 sections; ids follow p<part>c<chapter>s<n> using the given part/chapter numbers; each section must be writable from evidence (scenes from sessions, decisions, failures, code structure) — no filler; the LAST section should land the chapter's point and hand off to the next chapter. JSON only."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"545e2de1-748f-4926-8105-c86a97f4e28a","timestamp":"2026-07-02T20:18:20.724Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo","sessionId":"79f3f47a-9f9d-4a1f-b922-ef7b2aa390a9","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"545e2de1-748f-4926-8105-c86a97f4e28a","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\scripts\\longview\\prompts\\vampire_section.md","snippet":"1\tYou are writing ONE section of \"The AI Vampire\" — narrative nonfiction about a senior software engineer and multi-agent coordination, grounded in real session evidence. You are given: the book's metaphor and arc, the chapter brief, this section's spec, retrieved evidence (session chunks, notes, graph concepts), and the tail of the previous section for continuity.\n2\t\n3\tWrite the section in markdown, starting with `### <section title>`.\n4\t\n5\tCraft rules:\n6\t\n7\t- Narrative nonfiction voice: scenes, tension, specifics — not a report. Show the engineer at the keyboard, the agents at work, the failures as they happened.\n8\t- Weave the vampire metaphor with restraint — a thread, not a costume.\n9\t- Every load-bearing factual claim carries an inline citation: (sid: abc123) for sessions, (concept: X) for graph concepts, (doc: name) for documents. 2-5 citations per section.\n10\t- Technical substance is the point: real decisions, real trade-offs, real numbers where the evidence has them. Never invent events, quotes, or numbers.\n11\t- 650-950 words. End with a sentence that pulls the reader forward."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"04675347-900e-4fc9-92c0-4cc494fe37a9","timestamp":"2026-07-02T20:18:20.724Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo","sessionId":"79f3f47a-9f9d-4a1f-b922-ef7b2aa390a9","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"04675347-900e-4fc9-92c0-4cc494fe37a9","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\scripts\\longview\\lib\\opus.mjs","snippet":"1\t// The opus phase — \"The AI Vampire\": a book-length synthesis (200+ pages)\n2\t// built the only way a 4k-context local model can build one: hierarchically.\n3\t// One outline call (parts+chapters) → one sections call per chapter → one\n4\t// retrieval-grounded generation call per section (~90-110 sections), each\n5\t// bounded, each cited, each resume-safe (a section file on disk is done).\n6\t// Greater-than-the-sum comes from structure + retrieval, not context length.\n7\timport fs from \"fs\";\n8\timport path from \"path\";\n9\timport { fileURLToPath } from \"url\";\n10\timport { config, workspaceDir } from \"./config.mjs\";\n11\timport { chat, lastBalancedJson } from \"./llm.mjs\";\n12\timport { appendLedger, writeStatus } from \"./ledger.mjs\";\n13\timport { evidenceFor } from \"./retrieve.mjs\";\n14\t\n15\tconst __dirname = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\n16\tconst prompt = (name) =>\n17\t  fs.readFileSync(path.join(__dirname, \"..\", \"prompts\", `${name}.md`), \"utf8\");\n18\t\n19\tconst opusDir = (...p) => workspaceDir(\"data_out\", \"opus\", ...p);\n20\t\n21\tfunction readIf(p, cap = 4000) {\n22\t  try {\n23\t    return fs.readFileSync(p, \"utf8\").slice(0, cap);\n24\t  } catch {\n25\t    return \"\";\n26\t  }\n27\t}\n28\t\n29\tfunction foundationDigest() {\n30\t  const out = workspaceDir(\"data_out\");\n31\t  const parts = [\n32\t    `## Themes\\n${readIf(path.join(out, \"THEMES.md\"), 5000)}`,\n33\t    `## Portfolio report (excerpt)\\n${readIf(path.join(out, \"PORTFOLIO-REPORT.md\"), 2500)}`\n34\t  ];\n35\t  try {\n36\t    const dossiers = fs\n37\t      .readdirSync(path.join(out, \"dossiers\"))\n38\t      .filter((f) => f.endsWith(\".md\"))\n39\t      .map((f) => f.replace(/\\.md$/, \"\"));\n40\t    parts.push(`## Projects with dossiers\\n${dossiers.join(\", \")}`);\n41\t  } catch {\n42\t    /* none yet */\n43\t  }\n44\t  try {\n45\t    const notes = fs\n46\t      .readdirSync(path.join(out, \"discovery\"))\n47\t      .filter((f) => f.endsWith(\".md\"))\n48\t      .map((f) => \"- \" + readIf(path.join(out, \"discovery\", f), 120).split(\"\\n\")[0]);\n49\t    if (notes.length) parts.push(`## Discovery notes\\n${notes.join(\"\\n\")}`);\n50\t  } catch {\n51\t    /* none yet */\n52\t  }\n53\t  return parts.join(\"\\n\\n\");\n54\t}\n55\t\n56\tasync function jsonCall(name, system, user, maxTokens) {\n57\t  const started = Date.now();\n58\t  const res = await chat({ system, user, maxTokens, json: true, temperature: 0.5 });\n59\t  const parsed = lastBalancedJson(res.content);\n60\t  appendLedger({\n61\t    phase: \"opus\",\n62\t    artifact: name,\n63\t    ms: Date.now() - started,\n64\t    prompt_tokens: res.prompt_tokens,\n65\t    completion_tokens: res.completion_tokens,\n66\t    ok: Boolean(parsed)\n67\t  });\n68\t  return parsed;\n69\t}\n70\t\n71\tasync function buildOutline(interrupted) {\n72\t  const outlinePath = opusDir(\"outline.json\");\n73\t  let outline = null;\n74\t  try {\n75\t    outline = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(outlinePath, \"utf8\"));\n76\t  } catch {\n77\t    /* build it */\n78\t  }\n79\t  if (!outline) {\n80\t    console.log(\"[opus] outline: parts + chapters…\");\n81\t    outline = await jsonCall(\"outline\", prompt(\"vampire_outline\"), foundationDigest(), 2200);\n82\t    if (!outline?.parts?.length) throw new Error(\"outline did not parse — rerun the opus phase\");\n83\t    fs.writeFileSync(outlinePath, JSON.stringify(outline, null, 2));\n84\t  }\n85\t\n86\t  // Per-chapter section breakdown, resume-safe per chapter.\n87\t  for (const part of outline.parts) {\n88\t    for (const ch of part.chapters || []) {\n89\t      if (interrupted()) return outline;\n90\t      if (Array.isArray(ch.sections) && ch.sections.length) continue;\n91\t      console.log(`[opus] sections for part ${part.n} ch ${ch.n}: ${ch.title}`);\n92\t      const spec = await jsonCall(\n93\t        `sections:p${part.n}c${ch.n}`,\n94\t        prompt(\"vampire_chapter_sections\"),\n95\t        [\n96\t          `## Book\\n${JSON.stringify({ title: outline.title, metaphor: outline.metaphor, arc: outline.arc }).slice(0, 1500)}`,\n97\t          `## Part ${part.n}: ${part.title} — ${part.theme}`,\n98\t          `## Chapter (write sections for THIS one)\\n${JSON.stringify({ part: part.n, chapter: ch.n, title: ch.title, brief: ch.brief, projects: ch.projects, motifs: ch.motifs })}`,\n99\t          `## Evidence available\\n${foundationDigest().slice(0, 3000)}`\n100\t        ].join(\"\\n\\n\"),\n101\t        1400\n102\t      );\n103\t      if (spec?.sections?.length) {\n104\t        ch.sections = spec.sections;\n105\t        fs.writeFileSync(outlinePath, JSON.stringify(outline, null, 2));\n106\t      } else {\n107\t        console.log(\n108\t          `[opus] WARN sections for p${part.n}c${ch.n} did not parse — chapter will be regenerated on rerun`\n109\t        );\n110\t      }\n111\t    }\n112\t  }\n113\t  return outline;\n114\t}\n115\t\n116\tfunction allSections(outline) {\n117\t  const list = [];\n118\t  for (const part of outline.parts || []) {\n119\t    for (const ch of part.chapters || []) {\n120\t      for (const s of ch.sections || []) list.push({ part, ch, s });\n121\t    }\n122\t  }\n123\t  return list;\n124\t}\n125\t\n126\texport async function runOpus({ interrupted = () => false } = {}) {\n127\t  fs.mkdirSync(opusDir(\"sections\"), { recursive: true });\n128\t  const outline = await buildOutline(interrupted);\n129\t  const sections = allSections(outline);\n130\t  console.log(`[opus] ${sections.length} sections planned`);\n131\t  let done = 0,\n132\t    failed = 0;\n133\t\n134\t  for (const { part, ch, s } of sections) {\n135\t    const file = opusDir(\"sections\", `${s.id}.md`);\n136\t    if (fs.existsSync(file)) {\n137\t      done++;\n138\t      continue;\n139\t    }\n140\t    if (interrupted()) break;\n141\t    const started = Date.now();\n142\t    try {\n143\t      const evidence = await evidenceFor(s.query || `${ch.title} ${s.title}`, {\n144\t        topK: 4,\n145\t        budget: 3800\n146\t      });\n147\t      // Continuity: the tail of the previous section, if it exists.\n148\t      const idx = sections.findIndex((x) => x.s.id === s.id);\n149\t      let prevTail = \"\";\n150\t      if (idx > 0) {\n151\t        const prevFile = opusDir(\"sections\", `${sections[idx - 1].s.id}.md`);\n152\t        if (fs.existsSync(prevFile)) {\n153\t          const prev = fs.readFileSync(prevFile, \"utf8\");\n154\t          prevTail = prev.slice(-350);\n155\t        }\n156\t      }\n157\t      const res = await chat({\n158\t        system: prompt(\"vampire_section\"),\n159\t        user: [\n160\t          `## Book\\n${JSON.stringify({ metaphor: outline.metaphor, arc: outline.arc }).slice(0, 1200)}`,\n161\t          `## Chapter ${ch.n}: ${ch.title}\\n${ch.brief || \"\"}`,\n162\t          `## This section\\n${JSON.stringify({ title: s.title, brief: s.brief })}`,\n163\t          prevTail ? `## Previous section ends…\\n${prevTail}` : \"\",\n164\t          `## Retrieved evidence\\n${evidence}`\n165\t        ]\n166\t          .filter(Boolean)\n167\t          .join(\"\\n\\n\"),\n168\t        maxTokens: 1500,\n169\t        temperature: 0.65\n170\t      });\n171\t      const text = res.content.trim();\n172\t      if (text.length < 400) throw new Error(`section too short (${text.length} chars)`);\n173\t      fs.writeFileSync(file, text);\n174\t      done++;\n175\t      appendLedger({\n176\t        phase: \"opus\",\n177\t        artifact: `section:${s.id}`,\n178\t        ms: Date.now() - started,\n179\t        prompt_tokens: res.prompt_tokens,\n180\t        completion_tokens: res.completion_tokens,\n181\t        words: text.split(/\\s+/).length\n182\t      });\n183\t      console.log(\n184\t        `[opus] ${s.id} ok (${done}/${sections.length}, ${((Date.now() - started) / 1000).toFixed(0)}s)`\n185\t      );\n186\t    } catch (e) {\n187\t      failed++;\n188\t      appendLedger({\n189\t        phase: \"opus\",\n190\t        artifact: `section:${s.id}`,\n191\t        ok: false,\n192\t        error: String(e.message)\n193\t      });\n194\t      console.log(`[opus] ${s.id} FAILED — ${e.message} (rerun resumes here)`);\n195\t    }\n196\t    writeStatus({\n197\t      phase: \"opus\",\n198\t      opus_sections_done: done,\n199\t      opus_sections_total: sections.length,\n200\t      opus_failed: failed,\n201\t      current_section: s.id\n202\t    });\n203\t  }\n204\t\n205\t  // Assemble whatever exists — partial assemblies are useful previews and the\n206\t  // assembly is deterministic + idempotent.\n207\t  const words = assembleBook(outline);\n208\t  console.log(\n\n... [42 lines truncated] ..."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"31cef6db-b6e1-41f4-aab1-c7f4a49407c3","timestamp":"2026-07-02T20:18:20.725Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo","sessionId":"79f3f47a-9f9d-4a1f-b922-ef7b2aa390a9","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
