{"parentUuid":"3f5b89dc-06a2-4f1f-bab7-e7dc3ded3e1a","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\scripts\\longview\\prompts\\vampire_outline.md","snippet":"1\tYou are the structural editor of a book titled \"The AI Vampire\" — an intriguing, insightful work of narrative nonfiction about a senior software engineer and multi-agent coordination, grounded entirely in real evidence: months of working sessions, project dossiers, cross-project themes, and a code graph.\n2\t\n3\tDefine the vampire metaphor FROM THE EVIDENCE (e.g., agents that feed on context, tokens and attention; work that drains or is drained; the engineer learning to govern hungry processes with manifests, gates and honest ledgers — choose what the corpus actually supports). The book should read like a page-turner for technical readers: concrete scenes, hard-won engineering lessons, a genuine intellectual arc about coordinating machine collaborators.\n4\t\n5\tReturn ONLY this JSON (top level of the book — parts only, chapters come later):\n6\t\n7\t{\n8\t\"title\": \"The AI Vampire\",\n9\t\"subtitle\": \"...\",\n10\t\"metaphor\": \"2-3 sentences defining the vampire metaphor as used throughout\",\n11\t\"arc\": \"3-4 sentences: the narrative arc from the timeline evidence\",\n12\t\"parts\": [{ \"n\": 1, \"title\": \"...\", \"theme\": \"what this part explores and which projects/periods it draws on\" }]\n13\t}\n14\t\n15\tRules: 4-5 parts; grounded in the inputs; JSON only."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a08b2147-a764-404d-a81c-d343d0baa85d","timestamp":"2026-07-03T06:42:02.944Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"79f3f47a-9f9d-4a1f-b922-ef7b2aa390a9","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"a08b2147-a764-404d-a81c-d343d0baa85d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\scripts\\longview\\lib\\retrieve.mjs","snippet":"19\t      headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\", \"X-Benny-API-Key\": config.BENNY_API_KEY },\n20\t      body: JSON.stringify({ workspace: config.WORKSPACE, query, top_k: topK }),\n21\t      signal: AbortSignal.timeout(120000)\n22\t    });\n23\t    if (!res.ok) return [];\n24\t    const data = await res.json();\n25\t    const rows = Array.isArray(data) ? data : data.results || data.documents || [];\n26\t    return rows\n27\t      .map((r) => ({\n28\t        text: r.text || r.content || \"\",\n29\t        source: r.source || r.metadata?.source || \"\"\n30\t      }))\n31\t      .filter((r) => r.text);\n32\t  } catch {\n33\t    return [];\n34\t  }\n35\t}\n36\t\n37\t// Top concepts in the workspace graph — the weave phase samples these to keep\n38\t// discovery anchored to what the graph actually contains.\n39\texport async function graphCatalog(limit = 30) {\n40\t  try {\n41\t    const data = await bennyGet(\n42\t      `/api/graph/catalog?workspace=${encodeURIComponent(config.WORKSPACE)}`\n43\t    );\n44\t    const rows = Array.isArray(data) ? data : data.concepts || data.catalog || data.items || [];\n45\t    return rows\n46\t      .map((c) => (typeof c === \"string\" ? c : c.name || c.concept || \"\"))\n47\t      .filter(Boolean)\n48\t      .slice(0, limit);\n49\t  } catch {\n50\t    return [];\n51\t  }"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"79539c48-cca4-4480-93db-42ec3fb0fe8a","timestamp":"2026-07-03T06:42:02.944Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"79f3f47a-9f9d-4a1f-b922-ef7b2aa390a9","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"79539c48-cca4-4480-93db-42ec3fb0fe8a","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\scripts\\longview\\prompts\\vampire_section.md","snippet":"1\tYou are writing ONE section of \"The AI Vampire\" — narrative nonfiction about a senior software engineer and multi-agent coordination, grounded in real session evidence. You are given: the book's metaphor and arc, the chapter brief, this section's spec, retrieved evidence (session chunks, notes, graph concepts), and the tail of the previous section for continuity.\n2\t\n3\tWrite the section in markdown, starting with `### <section title>`.\n4\t\n5\tCraft rules:\n6\t\n7\t- Narrative nonfiction voice: scenes, tension, specifics — not a report. Show the engineer at the keyboard, the agents at work, the failures as they happened.\n8\t- Weave the vampire metaphor with restraint — a thread, not a costume.\n9\t- Every load-bearing factual claim carries an inline citation: (sid: abc123) for sessions, (concept: X) for graph concepts, (doc: name) for documents. 2-5 citations per section.\n10\t- Technical substance is the point: real decisions, real trade-offs, real numbers where the evidence has them. Never invent events, quotes, or numbers.\n11\t- 650-950 words. End with a sentence that pulls the reader forward."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"426ba3bf-340d-44c2-b888-bdfd91d9f823","timestamp":"2026-07-03T06:42:02.944Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"79f3f47a-9f9d-4a1f-b922-ef7b2aa390a9","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
